# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the CI ASan/UBSan gate.
#
# Vendored lsquic teardown: on abortive connection/engine destroy, lsquic
# releases QPACK decoder pages, bandwidth samplers and the cert cache only on
# the orderly drain path. These allocations live inside lib/lsquic, not CWIST
# code.
leak:lsquic_qdh_header_in_begin
leak:lsquic_malo_create
leak:lsquic_crt_init
leak:lsquic_bw_sampler_init
leak:lsquic_str_new
leak:lsquic_str_append
leak:lsquic_global_init
#
# CWIST HTTP/3 header-set (hsi_create) objects for streams that are still open
# when the engine is destroyed: lsquic never calls hsi_discard_header_set on
# the abortive teardown path. Tracked in ROADMAP.md ("Known limits"); fix
# belongs in the h3 stream-teardown path, after which this entry must go.
leak:cwist_h3_hsi_create
